{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600134",
      "title": "Redux vs React Context",
      "sourceHash": "781f9d40b3552c4e092a628aadccabeece1d975d82e7b3a41e40e39c6e359663",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.08,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "So Redux is a state management system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 8.06,
          "en": "for cross-component or app-wide state as we learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.06,
          "end": 10.34,
          "en": "And of course we can then ask ourselves,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.34,
          "end": 13.83,
          "en": "but don't we have React Context for that already?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.83,
          "end": 16.53,
          "en": "React Context is a concept and a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.53,
          "end": 18.1,
          "en": "we already alerted about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.1,
          "end": 20.63,
          "en": "and which we already used a lot in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.63,
          "end": 24.24,
          "en": "because it also allows us to avoid prop chains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.24,
          "end": 28.11,
          "en": "or prop drilling, and instead we can have a central place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.11,
          "end": 31.07,
          "en": "our Context and the Context Provider component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.07,
          "end": 33.37,
          "en": "which we use for managing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.37,
          "end": 35.81,
          "en": "So why do we need Redux?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.81,
          "end": 40.3,
          "en": "React Context has a couple of potential disadvantages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.3,
          "end": 43.99,
          "en": "And I say potential because they might not matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.99,
          "end": 45.49,
          "en": "in the app you're building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.49,
          "end": 47.99,
          "en": "And if they don't matter, you don't need Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.99,
          "end": 49.73,
          "en": "It is as simple as that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.73,
          "end": 53.06,
          "en": "And just as a side note, because it's all is important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.06,
          "end": 56.81,
          "en": "it's also not an either or decision.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.81,
          "end": 60.13,
          "en": "You can also use both Contexts and Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.13,
          "end": 62.13,
          "en": "in the same application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.13,
          "end": 64.23,
          "en": "Typically for application wide-state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.23,
          "end": 66.28,
          "en": "you will only use one of the two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.28,
          "end": 68.11,
          "en": "but then you could be using Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.11,
          "end": 70.8,
          "en": "for the general application wide-state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.8,
          "end": 75.8,
          "en": "and still use Context for selected multi-component states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.69,
          "end": 80.68,
          "en": "which are important in parts of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.68,
          "end": 84.45,
          "en": "So mixing and matching like that would also be possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 86.33,
          "en": "but let's not dive into that right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.33,
          "end": 89.26,
          "en": "let's instead focus on the disadvantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.26,
          "end": 91.82300000000001,
          "en": "you could be facing with React Context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.72,
          "end": 95.57,
          "en": "But what are these disadvantages then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.57,
          "end": 100.37,
          "en": "One potential disadvantage is that with React Context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.37,
          "end": 103.6,
          "en": "you can have a very complex setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.6,
          "end": 106.52000000000001,
          "en": "and managing state with React Context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.52000000000001,
          "end": 109.24000000000001,
          "en": "can become quite complex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.24000000000001,
          "end": 111.34,
          "en": "And that definitely depends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.34,
          "end": 113.83,
          "en": "on the kind of application you're building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.83,
          "end": 117.57,
          "en": "For a lot of small or medium-sized applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.57,
          "end": 120.58,
          "en": "that will very likely not be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.58,
          "end": 122.83,
          "en": "But if you're building a large application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.83,
          "end": 126.09,
          "en": "an enterprise level application with a lot of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.09,
          "end": 128.12,
          "en": "and a lot of things going on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.12,
          "end": 130.34,
          "en": "then when using React Context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.34,
          "end": 133.6,
          "en": "you can end up with code like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.6,
          "end": 136.46,
          "en": "Where you have a lot of different pieces of Context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.46,
          "end": 140.23,
          "en": "a lot of different States that affect multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.23,
          "end": 142.62,
          "en": "or the entire app, and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.62,
          "end": 145.31,
          "en": "a lot of different Context Provider components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.31,
          "end": 148.65,
          "en": "which you built for managing these states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.65,
          "end": 152.3,
          "en": "And you can end up with deeply nested JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.3,
          "end": 154.81,
          "en": "like this as a result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.81,
          "end": 156.66,
          "en": "Of course you don't need to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.66,
          "end": 159.2,
          "en": "a lot of different Context Providers though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.2,
          "end": 161.92000000000002,
          "en": "you could just use one big Context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.92000000000002,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "and one Context Provider component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 166.97,
          "en": "for a managing the entire state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.97,
          "end": 171.48,
          "en": "and all the different kinds of state of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.48,
          "end": 175.42000000000002,
          "en": "But that could lead in a large Context Provider component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.42000000000002,
          "end": 177.95,
          "en": "which manages a lot of different things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.95,
          "end": 180.66,
          "en": "and therefore itself becomes quite difficult",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.66,
          "end": 185.66,
          "en": "to maintain and manage because it's doing a lot of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.73,
          "end": 188.49,
          "en": "You might end up with a large Context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.49,
          "end": 193.09,
          "en": "that cares about authentication, theming, user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.09,
          "end": 195.11,
          "en": "if a modal should be displayed or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.11,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "and maybe a lot of other things as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 199.72,
          "en": "So, that could be a downside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.72,
          "end": 202.41,
          "en": "And if you split it into multiple Contexts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.41,
          "end": 205.32,
          "en": "you might be back to this picture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.32,
          "end": 207.32999999999998,
          "en": "So that can be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.32999999999998,
          "end": 210.35,
          "en": "And we haven't faced it thus far in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.35,
          "end": 213.48,
          "en": "because we definitely didn't build a large enterprise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213.48,
          "end": 216.7,
          "en": "level application in this course at this point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.7,
          "end": 219.89,
          "en": "But you can absolutely face this problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.89,
          "end": 223.12,
          "en": "in real react projects you might be working on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.12,
          "end": 226.7,
          "en": "and therefore this is one potential disadvantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.7,
          "end": 230.523,
          "en": "Another potential disadvantage could be performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.49,
          "end": 236.03,
          "en": "We have an official quote by a member of their React team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.03,
          "end": 239.65,
          "en": "who basically says that the new Context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.65,
          "end": 242.22,
          "en": "which is the Context you learn about in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 242.22,
          "end": 246.34,
          "en": "the post is from 2018, end of 2018,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.34,
          "end": 249.65,
          "en": "but still that is exactly the Context we are using here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.65,
          "end": 252.52,
          "en": "that this Context which was introduced back then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.52,
          "end": 254.79,
          "en": "which is why to post is from that date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.79,
          "end": 258.63,
          "en": "that this Context is great for low-frequency updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 258.63,
          "end": 262.92,
          "en": "like changing a theme, or maybe also authentication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.92,
          "end": 266.17,
          "en": "but it's not that great if your data changes a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.17,
          "end": 268.31,
          "en": "For a high frequency changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.31,
          "end": 271.67,
          "en": "though it's not clear what exactly high-frequency means,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.67,
          "end": 275.46,
          "en": "but for changes that happen more frequently or often general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 275.46,
          "end": 278.04,
          "en": "that it's not that good for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 280.37,
          "en": "And this team member says that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 280.37,
          "end": 284.15999999999997,
          "en": "therefore this new context is not ready",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 284.15999999999997,
          "end": 287.93,
          "en": "as a replacement for flux like state propagation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 287.93,
          "end": 289.7,
          "en": "Now this might not tell you much",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 289.7,
          "end": 294.36,
          "en": "but Redux is a flux like state management library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.36,
          "end": 296.68,
          "en": "So he says that React Context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.68,
          "end": 299.38,
          "en": "is not really a great replacement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 299.38,
          "end": 303.413,
          "en": "for Redux in all scenarios, in all cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.83,
          "end": 307.2,
          "en": "So therefore that's our second disadvantage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.2,
          "end": 310.47,
          "en": "performance can be bad if you're managing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.47,
          "end": 314.3,
          "en": "the wrong kinds of state with React Context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 314.3,
          "end": 316.3,
          "en": "Now, therefore to sum it up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 316.3,
          "end": 319.87,
          "en": "we have the complex setup and management disadvantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 319.87,
          "end": 323.69,
          "en": "because we may end up with deeply nested JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 323.69,
          "end": 326.5,
          "en": "and a lot of different Context Providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.5,
          "end": 330.86,
          "en": "or with one huge Context Provider which is not maintainable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 330.86,
          "end": 333.79,
          "en": "On the other hand we have potential performance issues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 333.79,
          "end": 336.07,
          "en": "because we should not use React Context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 336.07,
          "end": 338.99,
          "en": "for high-frequency state changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 338.99,
          "end": 342.3,
          "en": "Now I will, again, emphasize that for small",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 342.3,
          "end": 346.42,
          "en": "or medium-sized apps and even certainty a lot of big apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 346.42,
          "end": 348.62,
          "en": "this might all not matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 348.62,
          "end": 350.86,
          "en": "but of course my goal with the course here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 350.86,
          "end": 353.7,
          "en": "is to teach you realistic React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 353.7,
          "end": 356.35,
          "en": "which you can apply to any kind of project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 356.35,
          "end": 358.25,
          "en": "And therefore it is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 358.25,
          "end": 362.09,
          "en": "to be aware of these limitations of React Context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 362.09,
          "end": 366.11,
          "en": "which could matter in the projects you are working on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 366.11,
          "end": 368.56,
          "en": "And that's exactly why in this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 368.56,
          "end": 372.18,
          "en": "we are learning about an alternative to React Context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 372.18,
          "end": 374.13,
          "en": "We are learning about Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 374.13,
          "end": 377.33299999999997,
          "en": "which does not suffer from these disadvantages.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}